WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.880
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 6 is out,
let’s have a look.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.850
Beyond the Wall, Meera desperately tries to
outrun the wights, dragging Bran along behind

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.850
her.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.670
You gotta admire her loyalty – instead of
dumping Bran and saving herself, she continues

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.119
to risk her life to protect him.

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:19.749
She must really believe what the “raven”
claims – that Bran is important for the

00:00:19.749 --> 00:00:25.210
war to come against the white walkers . Anyway
while Meera does all the work, Bran is tripping

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.669
balls, having visions of the future and past.

00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:32.460
He sees winter and weirwoods and ravens, which
are associated with greensight – the magic

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.780
of his visions.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.030
He sees Daenerys and her dragons, including
one shot of a dragon flying over King’s

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.030
Landing.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.320
He sees wights, and white walkers, and the
Night King, and the Night King’s creation

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.359
by the children of the forest.

00:00:44.359 --> 00:00:47.890
He sees that one time a white walker took
a baby to the far north and the Night King

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.760
seemed to convert it into a walker.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.269
He sees the fall that crippled him, and the
deaths of his parents and his brother, he

00:00:54.269 --> 00:00:57.601
sees what’s inside the Tower of Joy – we’ll
have to wait til Episode 10 to see more.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:03.929
And he sees Aerys Targaryen, the father of
Daenerys and Viserys and Rhaegar.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:07.910
Aerys ruled as the King of Westeros before
Robert, but he “was mad and cruel” , he

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:12.490
loved to burn people alive , in fact one of
the people he burned was Rickard Stark, the

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.500
father of Ned Stark, who we saw last episode.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.430
Rickard’s death was one of the events that
led houses Arryn, Stark and Tully to rally

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.970
behind Robert Baratheon and rebel against
Aerys.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:27.430
The climax of this war was when Robert Baratheon
killed Aerys’ heir Prince Rhaegar at the

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.540
Battle of the Trident.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:33.420
But Aerys himself didn’t die until the later
Sack of King’s Landing, when Tywin Lannister

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.040
marched on the capital.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.009
During this battle, Aerys was killed by his
own Kingsguard, a young Jaime Lannister.

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:44.649
He murdered the king he was sworn to protect,
then he sat on the Iron Throne, waiting “to

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:49.479
see who would come to claim the kingdom”
. We learn in Season 3, in that amazing bath

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:54.039
scene, that the reason why Jaime killed Aerys
is that Aerys had secretly placed caches of

00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:59.000
wildlife all over King’s Landing – wildfire
is that explosive green stuff Tyrion used

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.359
to blow up Stannis’ fleet – so Jaime learned
that Aerys was planning to burn down King’s

00:02:04.359 --> 00:02:09.100
Landing – Jaime saved the city by killing
Aerys, but the thing is, those caches of wildfire

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:14.580
are still down there, a powder keg right under
the capital just waiting for a spark – and

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.959
in Bran’s vision, he foresees them exploding.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:21.540
Some readers believe that Cersei will try
to light the wildfire, and that Jaime will

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.140
have to kill her to stop her – fulfilling
the valonqar prophecy.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:29.370
But this shot, of what’s probably Dany’s
dragon Drogon over the city, suggests that

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.510
it might be dragonfire that sets off the wildfire.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.930
However it happens, by the time Dany takes
the capital, there might not be much of a

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.150
city left to rule...

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.680
Anyway after all these visions, Bran unplugs
from the Matrix and finds the wights are right

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.630
behind em, it looks like they’re gonna die,
but then they’re saved by a strange figure

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.550
in black…

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.540
Down in the Reach, Sam and Gilly head for
Horn Hill, Sam’s family home, and this is

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.640
amazing for Gilly.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.390
All she’s ever known before is Craster’s
Keep and Castle Black, such bleak, cold places,

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:01.150
so the south is “a whole new world” for
her.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.190
Sam is very nervous – he’s bringing his
girlfriend home to meet his parents, and while

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:09.400
his mother and sister are lovely, his father
is an abusive asshole who threatened to kill

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.549
him for not being manly enough.

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:15.629
Also he has to lie about Gilly’s son and
say it’s his, when it’s actually Craster’s,

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:19.900
and he has to hide the fact that Gilly is
a wildling, so this homecoming is a stressful

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.099
one for Sam.

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:25.019
In King’s Landing, Tommen talks with the
High Sparrow, and Tommen is surprisingly cool

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:28.860
with the idea of his wife Margaery being paraded
naked through the city.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.580
The Sparrow lets Tommen see Margaery, and
Marge appears to have given in to the High

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.049
Sparrow’s brainwashing.

00:03:34.049 --> 00:03:38.720
She says she once lied to make herself seem
sweet and kind, but now she’s found her

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.519
faith – “the gods have a plan for us all”.

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:45.709
Has Marge really suddenly become a good little
Christian?

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:49.050
In Episode 4 she seemed not at all convinced
by the Sparrow.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:53.459
But she did see her beloved brother Loras
suffering, so maybe Margaery realised she

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:58.720
needed a change in strategy – maybe she
figures if she plays along with the sparrows,

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.480
she could get into a position to strike.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:05.060
Back at Horn Hill, Gilly and Sam have an awkward
dinner with Sam’s family.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.680
Sam mentions Gilly is a good hunter, and Randyll
disapproves – he’s got strong ideas about

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.760
what women should and shouldn’t do – in
the books he meets Brienne and calls her a

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.780
“freak of nature” and a curse upon her
father , for wanting to fight and be a knight.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:23.210
Randyll finds out Gilly is a wildling, so
he calls her a savage and a wildling whore.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.920
He goes on a rant about how Sam’s a piece
of shit for not being a big tough warrior,

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:31.380
and while he allows Gilly and her baby to
stay at Horn Hill, he kicks Sam out of his

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.380
home.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:36.160
So Sam says farewell to Gilly, but then impulsively
changes his mind and decides to bring Gilly

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:41.060
and young Sam with him, and on his way out,
he takes Heartsbane, Randyll’s priceless

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:43.300
Valyrian steel greatsword, which…

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.030
seems a really bad idea.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:51.050
Heartsbane is the Freudian pride of Randyll’s
house, there is no doubt Randyll will come

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.050
for it.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.970
And what’s Sam even planning to do with
it?

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:58.120
Valyrian steel can apparently kill white walkers,
but Sam’s not going back to the Wall until

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.080
he’s studied at the Citadel for a while.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.080
And what about Gilly?

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.940
It’s very romantic to take her with him,
but she was offered a place at Horn Hill,

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:09.260
the safest place she’s likely to get to
stay, is it really fair on her or her infant

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.400
child to take her away from that?

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.040
Sam better have a plan here.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.160
Over in Braavos, Arya sees that play again
– with their version of the Purple Wedding,

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.080
with the pie, the wine, when Joffrey dies,
and Tywin’s death by Tyrion.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.730
Arya enjoys seeing Joffrey die – she’s
wanted to kill him for a long time.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:31.800
But Cersei, played by Lady Crane, gives a
speech about her grief at her son’s death,

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.370
and Arya seems moved.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.940
Maybe she wonders if killing really is the
right thing to do.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.870
She does poison Lady Crane’s rum anyway,
but then she bumps into her on the way out,

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:44.760
and they chat, and they connect over their
shared experience in acting.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.600
Crane asks her name and Arya says Mercy.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.030
So later, Mercy shows mercy, running back
and stopping Crane from drinking the poison

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.250
at the last minute.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.430
So here Arya makes her choice.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:59.900
She refuses to give up her sense of what’s
right, she refuses to give up who she is – she

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:04.560
goes and gets Needle from its hiding place,
drawing it from stone like Excalibur, and

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.600
this represents her re-embracing her connection
to her family.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:12.560
In the books it says Needle is “Robb and
Bran and Rickon, her mother and her father,

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.820
even Sansa”.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:19.750
Needle is “Jon Snow’s smile” . She is
returning to her identity as Arya Stark.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.720
Which means she’s breaking from the Faceless
Men.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.190
The waif sees all this, and gets permission
from Jaqen to kill Arya.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:30.710
It’s interesting that the waif so obviously
wants to kill Arya – just look at that bloody

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:34.350
smirk – when, as a Faceless Man, she’s
meant to not care who she kills, she’s meant

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:38.780
to have no desires or personality, she’s
meant to be no one.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:41.710
So – is the waif breaking her own rules?

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:46.020
Maybe Arya will somehow exploit the waif’s
humanity to defeat her – cause she’s gonna

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:50.010
need some advantage – we’ve seen that
the waif is a better fighter than her.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.910
But however it goes down this is a big moment
– Arya’s finally leaving the Faceless

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:55.910
Men.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:58.970
In King’s Landing, Jaime and the Tyrells
come to confront the High Sparrow.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:03.400
Mace Tyrell, with his magnificent hat, gives
an unconvincing speech, then the High Sparrow

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.310
gives a great speech.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:09.590
He presents King Tommen, who he won over with
the help of Margaery, and announces that the

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:14.560
crown and the Faith have united as one – as
represented by the Kingsguard wearing crowns

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.180
within stars as their new symbol – which
is a bit like Stannis’ fiery stag – the

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.270
political symbol swallowed by the religious
one.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:27.510
So, in one brilliant move, the Sparrow has
merged his power with the power of the Throne,

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:32.710
he’s taken all authority away from his opponents,
by showing that the King is on his side, not

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:37.160
theirs, and he’s made a great show of this
in front of all the city, to win over the

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.620
common people.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.770
This is masterful political theatre.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.800
This humble priest has made himself the most
powerful man in the city, and look at his

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:48.120
smile – he knows exactly what he’s doing.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.830
Afterwards, Tommen removes Jaime from the
Kingsguard, which is a big deal.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:55.920
The Kingsguard is meant to be a lifelong position
– Jaime’s just the second person ever

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.710
to be kicked out, after Barristan.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:02.500
The guard has been Jaime’s life since he
was fifteen , so now he’ll really have to

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.740
re-examine who is and what’s he’s doing
with himself.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:11.630
Then Tommen tells Jaime that he’s being
sent to the riverlands, to help Walder Frey.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:15.780
Walder Frey is the Lord of the Twins, and
the host of the Red Wedding that killed Robb

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.950
and Catelyn in Season 3.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.580
Here we see him complaining because he lost
Riverrun to Tullys, and he commands his men

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.710
to take the castle back.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:28.520
Walder seems mostly motivated by pride – he
says he hated serving under the Tullys, says

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:33.240
everybody’s laughing at him, and he refuses
to die until their laughter chokes.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.700
There are lots of characters like this in
Game of Thrones.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:40.770
Men who so need to feel important and respected
and powerful that they rant at the people

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.070
around them, shit all over their sons, and
wage whole fucking wars.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:50.740
The dumb pride of powerful men has caused
terrible damage in Westeros, and in the real

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.740
world.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:56.150
We see “Black” Walder Frey, who cut Catelyn’s
throat, and “Lame” Lothar Frey, who stabbed

00:08:56.150 --> 00:09:00.530
Robb’s wife Talisa – we and can probably
expect these guys to meet a violent end one

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.890
way or another.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:02.890
We also see Edmure.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.900
Edmure is Catelyn’s brother and the head
of House Tully.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:10.940
The Red Wedding was his wedding and he’s
been imprisoned by the Freys ever since.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.641
So the Freys want Riverrun, which is currently
held by Brynden “Blackfish”, apparently

00:09:14.641 --> 00:09:19.050
with the support of the Mallisters, and the
Blackwoods, and the brotherhood without banners.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:23.550
Riverrun’s set up for a long siege, so Jaime’s
gonna try to break the siege by convincing

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:27.550
the Blackfish to give up the castle.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:30.830
We also know Brienne’s on her way to try
to recruit the Tullys, so it’ll be interesting

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.860
to see how Jaime and Brienne interact.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:37.870
We also get a scene between Jaime and Cersei
– at first Jaime wants to try to take on

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.900
the High Sparrow himself, but Cersei acts
as a voice of reason, telling Jaime how much

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.720
of a bad idea that would be.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:48.450
Cersei seems to have become more subdued this
season, she’s still really angry and hateful

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.280
but she’s less obvious about it, which honestly
probably only makes her more dangerous.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.620
Cersei mentions her upcoming trial by combat,
and she’s confident that her champion Robert

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:02.580
Strong will succeed – but who will fight
against him as the champion of the Faith?

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.970
Well – ain’t sayin he’s a grave digger,
but he ain’t gonna be Lancel.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.130
This fight will be huge.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:12.050
Back beyond the Wall, the mysterious figure
who saved Bran and Meera reveals himself to

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:16.460
be long lost Uncle Benjen – and he’s looking
worse for wear.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:20.310
He says he was stabbed in the gut by a white
walker and left to die, but then the children

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:24.080
of the forest stabbed his heart with a blade
of dragonglass which apparently has turned

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.910
him into some kind of zombie.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:30.090
It’s not clear how exactly that all works,
but the point seems to be that he’s now

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:35.030
become a lot like the book character Coldhands,
a kind of friendly walking corpse.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.960
Cause like Coldhands, Benjen now has black
hands, which in Coldhands’ case indicates

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:44.580
he’s dead – his blood has congealed in
his extremities because his heart has ceased

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:49.440
to beat . Also like Coldhands, this new Benjen
seems connected to the three-eyed raven and

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.520
the children of the forest, he seems to have
been serving them these last few years.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.760
But what exactly was he doing, and what else
does he know, and why did he join the Watch

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.210
in the first place?

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:01.280
Hopefully we’ll get answers soon.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:05.990
Anyway Benjen says Bran has now in some sense
become the three-eyed raven, he’s like an

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:10.680
avatar of the old gods, with all the powers
and the knowledge of the greenseers within

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:11.680
him.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:15.430
We still don’t quite know what this means
or how it’ll work, but we do know he has

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:19.800
great power – and that he’ll have to learn
to use it fast if he’s to stand against

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.240
the walkers.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.900
On the way to Meereen, Daenerys chats with
Daario.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:27.650
Apparently Dany needs a thousand ships to
carry her army to Westeros, and, well, who

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.330
do we know with a thousand ships?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.690
“Build me a thousand ships”.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:35.980
Daario also says that Dany’s not a ruler,
she’s a conqueror – and he’s totally

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:40.070
right – Dany isn’t much good at sitting
on a throne and being a politician and making

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:41.070
difficult decisions.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:46.620
What she’s great at is sacking cities, leading
armies, riding dragons, burning shit, and

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:51.620
as if to illustrate the point, she flies in
on Drogon, who is fucking huge now, and makes

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:55.630
a speech from dragonback about how she’ll
take over Westeros with her Dothraki behind

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:56.630
her.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.840
Which, y’know, sounds nice in a speech.

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:02.910
But we’ve seen what Dothraki conquest looks
like – it’s ugly.

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.350
Homes are burned and pillaged.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.310
People are raped and killed.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:08.940
Is this the kind of conquest that Daenerys
will lead?

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:13.410
She’s got three big dragons now, will she
use them to “burn them all”, just like

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:15.020
her father, the Mad King?

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.279
We’ll have to wait and see.

00:12:17.279 --> 00:12:21.200
So a lot happened this week – Benjen’s
a zombie, Arya left the Faceless Men, Dany

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.360
speaks from dragonback, the Sparrow makes
plays in the capital, Sam stands up to his

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:28.990
dad, the Siege of Riverrun is set-up, and
Bran binge-watches the last few seasons of

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.610
Thrones over weirwood-net.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:35.190
We’ve got themes of family, with Sam, and
Bran, and Benjen, and even Arya connecting

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.190
with her past.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:40.310
And we see some great political theatre with
Daenerys and the High Sparrow using symbols

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.070
of power to give themselves authority.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:46.910
So while there weren’t as many murders or
tits this episode, we’ve got some solid

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.090
exploration of identity and power.

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:51.090
Thanks for watching.

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:54.610
And thanks to all Patrons supporting this
channel on Patreon – including David Howe,

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:58.730
